  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far (config_019, acc=0.639) uses PCA n2000 as the RNA encoder with multiprofile, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion. All completed experiments used PCA n2000, so the RNA encoder axis is completely unexplored. Question: Does a learned single-cell RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improve over linear PCA when all other settings are held at their empirically best values? This is a clean, single-variable comparison (PCA vs. scvi) that isolates the contribution of learned RNA representation. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a fundamental design axis—PCA is a simple linear projection while scvi learns a nonlinear latent representation tailored to single-cell data. If scvi improves performance, it opens a productive direction (configs 031-039) and suggests further investment in learned encoders. If it does not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and redirects budget toward the image encoder axis (ViT-L) or other factors. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

